/-!
# Free quotients of the differentials of a local algebra in characteristic zero

Let `k` be a field of characteristic zero, `R` a local `k`-algebra with finitely generated
differentials, and `q : Ω[R⁄k] → Rᵈ` a surjection. This file proves the local algebra of the
differential smoothness criterion: `q` is an isomorphism as soon as

* its kernel vanishes at every minimal prime of `R`, and
* every prime `P` of `R` whose residue field has transcendence degree at least `d` over `k` is a
  minimal prime of `R`.

For the local ring `R = 𝒪_{X,x}` of a reduced scheme `X`, locally of finite type and pure of
dimension `d` over `k`, with `q` the stalk of a locally free quotient of rank `d` of `Ω_{X/k}`,
both conditions are geometric. The minimal primes of `R` are the generic points of the
irreducible components through `x`; as `k` is perfect, they lie in the smooth locus, where
`Ω_{X/k}` is locally free of rank `d`, so `q` is an isomorphism there. And the transcendence
degree of `κ(P)` is the dimension of the closure of the point `P`, which is at most `d`, with
equality only at generic points of components.

The proof follows Nobile. Coordinates `x₁, …, x_d ∈ R` with dual derivations `δᵢ` split
`Ω[R⁄k] = N ⊕ ker q` with `N` spanned by the `dxⱼ`
(`KaehlerDifferential.exists_coordinates_of_kaehler_surjection`). If `M = Ω[R⁄k] ⧸ N ≅ ker q` were
nonzero, a prime `P` minimal over its annihilator would keep the `xⱼ` algebraically independent
(`TauCeti.KaehlerDifferential.algebraicIndependent_mk_of_mem_minimalPrimes`), so `κ(P)` would have
transcendence degree at least `d` and `P` would be a minimal prime of `R`; but `P` lies in the
support of the finitely generated `M`, against the first condition. So `ker q = 0`.

If moreover `R` is Noetherian of dimension at least `d` with residue field formally étale over `k`,
for instance finite over `k`, then `Ω[R⁄k] ≅ Rᵈ` and the conormal isomorphism
`𝔪/𝔪² ≅ κ ⊗[R] Ω[R⁄k]` make `𝔪` generated by `d` elements, so `R` is regular
(`TauCeti.isRegularLocalRing_of_basis_kaehlerDifferential`).

Characteristic zero is needed. Over `𝔽₂` the local ring of the cusp `y² = x³` at the origin has
the free quotient `dx ↦ 0`, `dy ↦ 1` of rank one, whose kernel `R·dx` is killed by `x²`, hence
vanishes at the unique minimal prime, and both conditions hold; yet `q` is not injective and the
cusp is not regular.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.KaehlerDifferential.bijective_of_surjective_of_charZero`: in characteristic zero, a
  surjection `Ω[R⁄k] → Rᵈ` whose kernel vanishes at the minimal primes is bijective, provided the
  primes with residue field of transcendence degree at least `d` are minimal.
* `TauCeti.KaehlerDifferential.isRegularLocalRing_of_surjective_of_charZero`: under the same
  hypotheses, a Noetherian `R` of dimension at least `d` with formally étale residue field is a
  regular local ring.

## References

* A. Nobile, *Notes on Nash modification*, arXiv:2404.09102, Section 2, proof of
  Proposition 2.3.
-/

public section

open KaehlerDifferential IsLocalRing

namespace TauCeti.KaehlerDifferential

variable {k R ι : Type*} [Field k] [CharZero k] [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [Algebra k R]
  [Module.Finite R Ω[R⁄k]] [Finite ι]

/-- **A free quotient of the differentials is an isomorphism**, in characteristic zero. Let `R` be
a local algebra over a field `k` of characteristic zero, with finitely generated differentials, and
let `q : Ω[R⁄k] → (ι → R)` be surjective. Suppose that the kernel of `q` vanishes at every minimal
prime of `R`, and that every prime of `R` whose residue field has transcendence degree at least
`Nat.card ι` over `k` is a minimal prime. Then `q` is bijective, so `Ω[R⁄k]` is free of rank
`Nat.card ι`. -/
theorem bijective_of_surjective_of_charZero (q : Ω[R⁄k] →ₗ[R] ι → R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hmin : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum R, p.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes R →
      p ∉ Module.support R (LinearMap.ker q))
    (htrdeg : ∀ (P : Ideal R) [P.IsPrime],
      (Nat.card ι : Cardinal) ≤ Algebra.trdeg k P.ResidueField → P ∈ minimalPrimes R) :
    Function.Bijective q := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨x, δ, hδ, -, hcompl⟩ := exists_coordinates_of_kaehler_surjection q hq
  -- It suffices that the coordinate differentials `dxⱼ` span `Ω[R⁄k]`.
  suffices hN : Submodule.span R (Set.range (D k R ∘ x)) = ⊤ by
    refine ⟨LinearMap.ker_eq_bot.mp (top_disjoint.mp ?_), hq⟩
    rw [← hN]
    exact hcompl.disjoint
  by_contra hN
  set M := Ω[R⁄k] ⧸ Submodule.span R (Set.range (D k R ∘ x))
  have : Nontrivial M := Submodule.Quotient.nontrivial_iff.mpr hN
  -- A prime `P` minimal over the annihilator of `M` keeps the coordinates independent.
  have hann : Module.annihilator R M ≠ ⊤ := by
    rwa [Ne, Module.annihilator_eq_top_iff, not_subsingleton_iff_nontrivial]
  obtain ⟨P, hP, -⟩ := Ideal.exists_minimalPrimes_le (le_maximalIdeal hann)
  have := hP.1.1
  have hind := AlgebraicIndependent.map' (algebraicIndependent_mk_of_mem_minimalPrimes hδ hP)
    (f := IsScalarTower.toAlgHom k (R ⧸ P) P.ResidueField)
    (Ideal.injective_algebraMap_quotient_residueField P)
  -- So `κ(P)` has transcendence degree at least `Nat.card ι`, and `P` is a minimal prime of `R`.
  have hPmin : P ∈ minimalPrimes R := by
    refine htrdeg P ?_
    have h := hind.lift_cardinalMk_le_trdeg
    rwa [← Nat.cast_card, Cardinal.lift_natCast, Cardinal.nat_le_lift_iff] at h
  -- But `P` lies in the support of `M ≅ ker q`.
  refine hmin ⟨P, hP.1.1⟩ hPmin ?_
  rw [← (Submodule.quotientEquivOfIsCompl _ _ hcompl).support_eq]
  exact Module.mem_support_iff_of_finite.mpr hP.1.2

/-- **A free quotient of the differentials forces regularity**, in characteristic zero. Let `R`
be a Noetherian local algebra over a field `k` of characteristic zero, with finitely generated
differentials and residue field formally étale over `k`, for instance finite over `k`, and let
`q : Ω[R⁄k] → (ι → R)` be surjective. Suppose that the kernel of `q` vanishes at every minimal
prime of `R`, that every prime of `R` whose residue field has transcendence degree at least
`Nat.card ι` over `k` is a minimal prime, and that `R` has dimension at least `Nat.card ι`. Then
`R` is a regular local ring. -/
theorem isRegularLocalRing_of_surjective_of_charZero [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [Algebra.FormallyEtale k (ResidueField R)] (q : Ω[R⁄k] →ₗ[R] ι → R)
    (hq : Function.Surjective q)
    (hmin : ∀ p : PrimeSpectrum R, p.asIdeal ∈ minimalPrimes R →
      p ∉ Module.support R (LinearMap.ker q))
    (htrdeg : ∀ (P : Ideal R) [P.IsPrime],
      (Nat.card ι : Cardinal) ≤ Algebra.trdeg k P.ResidueField → P ∈ minimalPrimes R)
    (hdim : (Nat.card ι : WithBot ℕ∞) ≤ ringKrullDim R) :
    IsRegularLocalRing R :=
  isRegularLocalRing_of_basis_kaehlerDifferential
    ((Pi.basisFun R ι).map
      (LinearEquiv.ofBijective q (bijective_of_surjective_of_charZero q hq hmin htrdeg)).symm)
    hdim

end TauCeti.KaehlerDifferential
